The contents of this directory are licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.

This is deliberate and contained. `primer3-py` is GPLv2, and importing it makes
the importing code a derivative work. Everything that imports it lives here;
nothing here is imported by the Rust crates or by the web interface, which
reach this worker by running it as a separate process and reading its output.
That keeps the rest of PCRStudio under MIT.

